Job Description:
Job Description

As an HBO Intern focused on Automated Testing and AI Integration for Mainframe Finance, you will be part of the Mainframe Finance team and focus on automating the creation of change documentation for mainframe applications.

This internship consists of:

Gaining an understanding of the existing Tosca automation framework and Python workflows;
Developing and refining a documentation workflow in Visual Studio Code using Copilot, or researching alternative tools for generating test documentation;
Ensuring that generated documents accurately describe test steps, expected results, and captured evidence;
Handling test data and screenshots in accordance with company security and confidentiality requirements.

Your profile

You are enrolled in an HBO programme in IT, Business IT, Information Management, or a related field;
You are interested in automation, testing, AI, and process improvement;
You have an analytical mindset and enjoy structuring information;
You work accurately and independently;
You have good communication skills in English.

Department

The Mainframe Finance team is part of the IT organization at DAF Trucks and supports financially critical processes such as accounting, reporting, and financial controls. The team works on mainframe applications that require high levels of reliability, traceability, and documentation. To improve quality and efficiency, the department continuously looks for ways to automate and standardize processes. The goal of the department is to deliver stable, well-documented, and compliant financial IT solutions.

We offer

A look behind the scenes at a large, international organization; 
You get a lot of freedom and responsibility. We are open to your initiatives and depending on the assignment, you will see your results on the work floor; 
An experienced coach and mentor, from whom you can learn a lot and who is ready to help you further; 
An internship allowance of € 375 gross (Bachelor) or € 450 gross (Master) per month on a full-time basis; 
A travel allowance, if you do not possess a student travel product; 
A housing allowance, if you temporarily rent a room near DAF.

Every intern gets the chance to participate in the Student Event. During this event, you get to meet other interns and find out more about DAF/PACCAR! Curious about how students experience their internship at DAF? Read stories from our former interns here.

Please note: for non-EU students, the internship or graduation project must be part of your study program, and a tripartite agreement signed by the student, employer, and educational institution is required. A government-approved template can be found on the Nuffic website. Standard internship agreement for non-eu-eea students

Interested?

Upload your CV and cover letter via the apply button below. For more information, you can contact Paddy Wilms via Email paddy.wilms@paccar.com or phone number 040-2142616. 
